# Claude Hooks — {{ project_name }}

Hooks run automatically before or after Claude Code actions. They are enforcement — not suggestions.

## Hook Types

| Type | Trigger | Use For |
|------|---------|---------|
| `pre-bash` | Before shell command execution | Safety checks, dry-run guards |
| `post-bash` | After shell command execution | Logging, state sync |
| `pre-write` | Before file write | Lint, format, schema validation |
| `post-write` | After file write | Index updates, cache invalidation |
| `pre-task` | Before a task begins | Scope confirmation, context load |
| `post-task` | After a task completes | CHANGELOG update, notification |

## Files in This Directory

- `guardrail-check.sh` — Pre-bash safety gate. Block writes to protected paths and destructive operations.
- `changelog-update.sh` — Post-task CHANGELOG appender. Call after any significant change.

## Writing a New Hook

Exit codes:
- `0` — proceed
- `1` — block with error message to stderr
- `2` — block silently

Hooks receive the command or file path as `$1`.
